Excerpt from The Islamabad Rent Restriction Ordinance, 2001, Section 15 - Eviction of tenant:
(2) A landlord who seeks to evict his tenant shall apply to the Controller for an order in that behalf, and the Controller may, after giving the tenant a reasonable opportunity of showing cause against the application, make an order directing the tenant to put the landlord in possession, if he is satisfied that--
(i) the tenant has not paid or tendered rent due from him in respect of the building or rented land, within fifteen days after the expiry of the time fixed in the agreement of tenancy with his landlord, or in the absence of any such agreement, within sixty days from the period for which the rent is payable;
(ii) the tenant has, without the written consent of the landlord,--
(a) transferred his right under the lease or sublet the entire building or rented land or any portion thereof; or
(b) used the building or rented land for a purpose other than that for which it was leased;
(iii) the tenant has committed such acts as are likely to impair materially the value or utility of the building or rented land;
(iv) the acts and conduct of the tenant have been a nuisance to the occupiers of buildings in the neighbourhood;
(v) the landlord requires it in good faith for his own occupation or for the occupation of his spouse or any of his children.

